	"identifying_description": "After a painting by Francois Boucher (72.15), a beribboned shepherdess offers her lover a grape in a pastoral idyll. It is the reverse of the original, suggesting that this artist worked from an engraving. Costume and facial details also differ from the original. On the reverse shows a chinoiserie scene of a bearded scholar, attendant, and friend enjoying a garden of giant peonies with a grotesque rock.",
